id: interface/node
title: "interface node"
kind: mental-model-node
status: v0-seed
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Hold the five-command brain interface and projection stack.

holds:
  - mirror
  - map
  - meaning
  - move
  - memory
  - projection stack
  - shared YAWN chrome contract
  - shared brand and capability semantics
  - quiet public-root and progressively disclosed public-View shells
  - source-preserving + Yawn creation contract
  - coordinate-complete New Yawn grid over the canonical Orientation Map
  - local observation-question-art proposal chain
  - local observation-art generation contract
  - dialogue objective compiler and correction operators
  - one-question orientation_inquiry View with source-preserving selection and answer provenance
  - non-authoritative move proposals and rightful choice boundaries

receives:
  - lived signals
  - current frames
  - missing bridges
  - proof and replay needs

produces:
  - cognition handles
  - frame maps
  - movement choices
  - replay surfaces

questions:
  - what is here
  - what does it belong to
  - what is missing
  - what can move
  - what changed
  - what objective and structure did the system detect
  - why was this orientation question and presentation selected
  - what is settled, proposed, or still open at this coordinate
  - what intelligence is bound here without becoming identity or authority

